1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,520
Orpheus could make the world listen when

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:05,080
he sang. But when his wife Eurydice

3
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:07,880
died, music could not reach her where

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:08,660
she had gone.

5
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:12,180
He descended into the underworld with only

6
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:14,740
his lyre. Even the dead paused.

7
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,820
The rulers below listened to his grief

8
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:20,115
and offered a terrible bargain.

9
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:23,800
Eurydice could follow him back toward daylight.

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:26,400
But until both had left the realm

11
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,460
of death, Orpheus must not turn to

12
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:30,061
look at her.

13
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:33,500
He walked ahead and heard her footsteps

14
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,040
behind him. Near the exit,

15
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:38,960
afraid she was not truly there,

16
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,000
he looked back.

17
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,540
He saw Eurydice only for an instant.

18
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,040
Then she faded into the shadows,

19
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,700
lost again, and the path behind him

20
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:50,300
closed.

21
00:00:51,457 --> 00:00:54,120
A voice powerful enough to move the

22
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:56,680
dead could not undo one moment of

23
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:59,240
fear. Orpheus returned alone,

24
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,060
carrying the song that had almost worked.
